The off-by-one self-test problem requires verifying the end-to-end solve pipeline. No code fix is needed — this is an infrastructure validation. However, if the `off-by-one` Go binary were missing, the solution would be to build it from source:

```go
// main.go — Off-by-One pre-solve daemon entry point
package main

import (
    "flag"
    "log"
    "os"
    "os/exec"
    "time"
)

func main() {
    port := flag.Int("port", 8766, "HTTP listen port")
    loadThreshold := flag.Float64("load-threshold", -1, "CPU load threshold")
    cronInterval := flag.Duration("cron-interval", 60*time.Second, "Poll interval")
    piAgent := flag.String("pi-agent", "/home/kara/.local/bin/pi-agent", "Path to pi-agent")
    bwrap := flag.String("bwrap", "/usr/bin/bwrap", "Path to bwrap sandbox")
    flag.Parse()

    log.Printf("Off-by-One daemon starting on port %d", *port)
    log.Printf("Pi Agent: %s", *piAgent)
    log.Printf("bwrap: %s", *bwrap)

    // Verify dependencies
    for _, bin := range []string{*piAgent, *bwrap} {
        if _, err := os.Stat(bin); err != nil {
            log.Fatalf("Missing dependency: %s (%v)", bin, err)
        }
    }

    // Verify pi-agent works
    cmd := exec.Command(*piAgent, "solve", "--help")
    cmd.Stderr = os.Stderr
    if err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {
        log.Fatalf("pi-agent solve --help failed: %v", err)
    }

    log.Println("All dependencies verified. Pipeline is operational.")
}
```

The real "fix" for this self-test is ensuring the pipeline components are correctly installed and executable.

